{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00373",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 3.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. Where would you like me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.04,
      "end_seconds": 7.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Right, yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.64,
      "end_seconds": 22.79,
      "duration_seconds": 15.15,
      "text": "Right, I wanted to get a burning pain in the upper tummy looked at. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.49,
      "end_seconds": 28.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Alright, how long have you had it? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.93,
      "end_seconds": 36.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "It's been one week now. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.4,
      "end_seconds": 40.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.92,
      "end_seconds": 42.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.81,
      "end_seconds": 47.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Is there anything that triggers it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.95,
      "end_seconds": 52.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "It's worse with spicy food and an empty stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.61,
      "end_seconds": 56.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Have you found anything that eases it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.29,
      "end_seconds": 61.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "It settles a little with antacids."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.51,
      "end_seconds": 65.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.08,
      "end_seconds": 69.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.92,
      "end_seconds": 73.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.45,
      "end_seconds": 82.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "Well, when it starts I tend to get bloating after meals as well. The bloating after meals? That's been for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.68,
      "end_seconds": 87.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.54,
      "end_seconds": 93.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Yeah, mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.76,
      "end_seconds": 99.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Any black stools or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.9,
      "end_seconds": 102.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, um, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.86,
      "end_seconds": 105.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.25,
      "end_seconds": 118.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Hmm, um, I've had arthritis in my knees, yes. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.82,
      "end_seconds": 122.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.03,
      "end_seconds": 125.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "My brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.84,
      "end_seconds": 130.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.01,
      "end_seconds": 133.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.19,
      "end_seconds": 137.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.39,
      "end_seconds": 143.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Um, uh, I take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.62,
      "end_seconds": 144.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.65,
      "end_seconds": 146.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "It's Digene, when it burns."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.92,
      "end_seconds": 151.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.14,
      "end_seconds": 152.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.41,
      "end_seconds": 174.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.87,
      "end_seconds": 177.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.96,
      "end_seconds": 181.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Okay, do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.45,
      "end_seconds": 193.55,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.74,
      "end_seconds": 197.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.87,
      "end_seconds": 199.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.63,
      "end_seconds": 203.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.42,
      "end_seconds": 206.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.27,
      "end_seconds": 215.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No guarding and no lumps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.98,
      "end_seconds": 221.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.64,
      "end_seconds": 225.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.93,
      "end_seconds": 226.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.61,
      "end_seconds": 254.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. So, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with gastritis at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.23,
      "end_seconds": 257.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.34,
      "end_seconds": 278.25,
      "duration_seconds": 18.91,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's gastritis, and we'll know more once the an upper endoscopy is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a burning pain in the upper tummy for one week, mild, and no fever or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.99,
      "end_seconds": 281.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Yes, you know, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.92,
      "end_seconds": 285.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.4,
      "end_seconds": 318.93,
      "duration_seconds": 17.53,
      "text": "Alright, back to you. I'd like to arrange an upper endoscopy for persistent dyspepsia. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm prescribing pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, for four weeks. That's for gastritis. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.66,
      "end_seconds": 322.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.69,
      "end_seconds": 344.95,
      "duration_seconds": 22.26,
      "text": "Avoid spicy, oily food and don't take anti-inflammatory painkillers on an empty stomach. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Please don't sit on it if you vomit blood or pass black stools. That's the point to get seen urgently. I'd like to see you again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.98,
      "end_seconds": 347.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.33,
      "end_seconds": 352.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.03,
      "end_seconds": 360.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "So, I take the pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.74,
      "end_seconds": 366.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.11,
      "end_seconds": 371.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yeah, I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.27,
      "end_seconds": 374.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}